  "geometry_notes": "Meso tartaric acid, HO2C–CH(OH)–CH(OH)–CO2H. World scale: central C–C bond 1.6 units, drawn vertically along +Y with the upper carbon at (0, 0.8, 0) and lower at (0, -0.8, 0). Symmetry plane is a horizontal parallelogram in the y=0 plane, ~5 units wide (X) × 2 units deep (Z), pale blue #b9dff5 at ~45% opacity, edges slightly darker; it is perpendicular to the C–C bond and extends beyond the molecule on both sides. Upper carbon substituents (bond length 1.1): OH oxygen up-left at (-0.9, 1.4, 0.15) with its hydroxyl H beyond at (-1.5, 1.05, 0.3); H (small, 0.45× radius) down-right toward viewer at (0.55, 0.45, 0.85); carboxyl carbon up-right at (0.95, 1.4, -0.1), branching to two oxygens at (1.9, 1.15, 0.1) and (0.95, 2.4, -0.3) plus a small acid H. Lower carbon substituents are the exact mirror images through y=0 (negate Y of every upper-half position). Colors: carbon dark gray #4b5058; stereocenter hydrogens pale blue #7cc0e8; hydroxyl oxygen and its hydrogen red/dark red #b23225 and #8f231a; entire CO2H branch rendered green #3fbf5c (matching the green CO2H label in the 2D panel); bonds light gray #c9ced4 cylinders of radius 0.09, with a glossy specular highlight on each sphere. Sphere radii: C 0.38, O 0.34, green carboxyl atoms 0.34, H 0.20. 2D panel (shown in the same scene, offset to screen-left by ~4.5 units, drawn flat facing the camera in the XY plane): two black 'C' letters at (-4.5, 0.55) and (-4.5, -0.55); vertical plain bond between them; upper C has a short dashed vertical bond up to blue 'H' (#1f8fc2) at (-4.5, 1.25), a bold solid wedge left to magenta 'HO' (#d4197f) at (-5.5, 0.9), a plain bond right to green 'CO2H' (#127a4a) at (-3.4, 0.9); lower C mirrors this with the dashed bond and 'H' pointing down. A pale blue edge-on parallelogram at y=0 spans x from -5.6 to -3.6, with black text 'Symmetry plane' to its right at (-2.6, 0). Highlight color for clicked/partner groups: warm yellow glow #ffd24d outline.",
